# NextBus HK — every environment variable in the repo, in one place.
#
# ┌─ READ THIS FIRST ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ **Nothing loads a `.env` file from the repo root.** Copying this file to `.env` here has no  │
# │ effect on any build. It is an *inventory*, not a configuration: the full list of variables   │
# │ this repo reads, with each one's default and who reads it, so that "drop in the real domain" │
# │ is one lookup rather than a grep. The real homes are:                                       │
# │                                                                                             │
# │   apps/mobile/.env.local     Expo — loads `.env*` from ITS OWN directory (see .env.example)  │
# │   apps/web/.env.local        Vite — same, from `apps/web/` (see .env.example)                │
# │   apps/edge/.dev.vars        Wrangler — the Worker's own vars for `wrangler dev`             │
# │   GitHub → Actions           the CI credentials; never a file (docs/10)                      │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# The canonical table, with the reasoning, is docs/10 "Configuration & secrets" (ADR-061).
# **A fresh clone needs none of this.** Every upstream we consume is keyless; `pnpm dev` works with
# nothing configured. The only credentials that exist let CI *publish* the dataset.

# ── The app shells: one variable per renderer, and that is the whole point ─────────────────────
# Base URL of the edge Worker. Unset ⇒ `DEFAULT_API_URL` in `packages/api-client/src/endpoint.ts`,
# which is the ONE declaration of `http://localhost:8787` (there were four copies before Wave 5;
# `scripts/check-one-endpoint-declaration.mjs` now fails the build if a second one appears).
#
# The **live socket URL is derived from this**, not configured: `liveSocketUrl` in `@nextbus/core`
# maps `http:`→`ws:` / `https:`→`wss:` and appends `/v1/live` (ADR-056 decision 8). So the day the
# domain exists, this is the only line that changes — per renderer, not per capability.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the JS bundle and readable in DevTools. Never a credential.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# ── Reserved: the socket escape hatch, and the engine selector ─────────────────────────────────
# **Nothing reads either of these yet.** They are documented because the plumbing they would use is
# already there and named, and because a reader who finds `EdgeClientOptions.liveUrl` /
# `EdgeClientOptions.transport` should be able to tell "wired but unset" from "not wired". Wiring
# them is one line per app shell — see WP5-6 in docs/proposals/03 and ADR-056 §"What is not done".
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_URL / VITE_LIVE_URL — an explicit socket URL, for the one case derivation cannot
# cover: a socket tier on a different host. Passed to `EdgeClientOptions.liveUrl`, which exists.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_URL=wss://live.example.test/v1/live
# VITE_LIVE_URL=wss://live.example.test/v1/live
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_TRANSPORT / VITE_LIVE_TRANSPORT — `poll` (the shipped default: HTTP polling
# wearing the frame protocol) or `socket` (the real `/v1/live` shard). There is deliberately no
# `auto`: an automatic choice implies a fallback from socket to poll, and no such fallback exists —
# `createSocketTransport` reconnects for ever rather than degrading, so `auto` would be a promise
# the code does not keep.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVE_TRANSPORT=poll
# VITE_LIVE_TRANSPORT=poll

# ── The Worker's own vars (apps/edge/.dev.vars locally; `[vars]` in wrangler.toml when deployed) ─
# LIVE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS — comma-separated browser origins allowed to open `/v1/live`. Unset ⇒ **no
# filtering at all**, which is the default and is stated plainly rather than dressed up: there is no
# production origin to allowlist until WP0-5, and a WebSocket upgrade does not honour CORS, so this
# check is browser-only and advisory in any case (ADR-056 decision 9). A missing `Origin` header is
# always allowed — that is what native clients send.
# LIVE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://nextbus.example,https://www.nextbus.example

# ── CI and deploy: none of these exist yet (WP0-5) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set as GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions. Not files, and not in `wrangler.toml`.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN   secret    — `dataset:publish` and `wrangler deploy`. Scope: Workers Scripts
#                                    + KV Edit + R2 Edit, one account. Not the Global API Key.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  secret    — an identifier, but treat it as one anyway.
# DATASET_PUBLISH_ARMED  variable  — `true` once the KV namespace exists; until then the nightly
#                                    dataset publish self-skips instead of failing every night.
# EDGE_URL               variable  — e.g. `https://api.example.test`. The deployed Worker, for the
#                                    `/v1/health` acceptance check (`"dataset":"kv"` with
#                                    `datasetBuildsThisIsolate: 0`). Unset ⇒ that check is SKIPPED
#                                    and both workflows say so in the log, because a gate that
#                                    silently did not run is this repo's recurring failure.
